    "body": "Fixes #7500\n\nOptimised comparisons and comparisons used as booleans generate a C `bint` but call Python C-API helpers such as `PyUnicode_Compare`, `PyDict_Contains` and `__Pyx_PyObject_RichCompareBool`, so they cannot run without the GIL\n\nThe `nogil` check only inspected the result type and thus missed them whenever the result was coerced to `bint`\n\nReject these comparisons in `nogil` sections, while keeping pointer comparisons, `is` / `is not` checks and `in` checks on C pointer slices valid\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/8146#discussion_r4626694150"
                },
                "pull_request": {
